{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1552 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8917643137478667ef1be43b5cfbb7ae9819d45037a7b89dd1ad1616f97abcd1" :edb/db-before-t 1551 :edb/db-after-t 1552 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534864 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:14:59.158Z" 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186130744 1075 #edb/ref 17592186130745 13194139534864 17592186045417 false] [17592186130744 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441592 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186130744 1078 #edb/ref 17592186130747 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186133886 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441617 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186133886 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441618 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186133900 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441615 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186133900 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441616 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186134098 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186134098 1071 "![](images/72/7264984a1c19c247c030feae04615bb0c46205ca70475db1240db964ad6007b2.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on $R^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that\n\n$∮_(C_{1})F \\cdot dr = 10, ∮_(C_{2})F \\cdot dr =-4, ∮_(C_{3})F \\cdot dr =-2$,\n\nwhere $C_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and $C_{2}$ and $C_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $∮_(∂D)F \\cdot dr$." 13194139534864 17592186045417 false] [17592186134098 1071 "![](images/72/7264984a1c19c247c030feae04615bb0c46205ca70475db1240db964ad6007b2.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=10,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-4,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-2,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186134098 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/0d/0de833fcc39b6295418c1558cf1187774db7b4ada1d697f2dcac8c35858563df.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =10-4-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1043 #edb/ref 17592186441619 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1043 #edb/ref 17592186441620 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1043 #edb/ref 17592186441621 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1043 #edb/ref 17592186441622 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1043 #edb/ref 17592186441623 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1045 "Extending Green's Theorem" 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1046 #edb/ref 17592186441620 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050560 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441589 1053 #uuid "12c751f0-6856-54db-a651-f054b3719043" 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441590 1080 "\\frac{89}{3}" 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441590 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534864 17592186045417 true] [17592186441590 1083 #uui